home_content_abj
Simple by design. Powerful by default.
-----
home_content_aca
The language gets out of your way.
-----
home_content_acb
You can learn the entire language by going through the
-----
home_content_acc
documentation
-----
home_content_acd
over a weekend, and in most cases there's only one way to do something.
-----
home_content_ace
This results in simple, readable, and maintainable code.
-----
home_content_acf
Despite being simple, V gives a lot of power to the developer and can be used in pretty much every field, including systems programming, webdev, gamedev, GUI, mobile, science, embedded, tooling, etc.
-----
home_content_acg
V is very similar to Go. If you know Go, you already know ≈80% of V. Things V improves on Go:
-----
home_content_ach
vlang.io/compare#go
-----
home_content_aci
Safety
-----
home_content_acj
Bounds checking
-----
home_content_ada
No undefined values
-----
home_content_adb
No variable shadowing
-----
home_content_adc
Immutable variables by default
-----
home_content_add
Immutable structs by default
-----
home_content_ade
Option/Result and mandatory error checks
-----
home_content_adf
Sum types
-----
home_content_adg
Generics
-----
home_content_adh
Immutable function args by default, mutable args have to be marked on call
-----
home_content_adi
No null
-----
home_content_adj
(allowed in unsafe code)
-----
home_content_aea
No undefined behavior
-----
home_content_aeb
new!
-----
home_content_aec
No global variables
-----
home_content_aed
(can be enabled for low level apps like kernels via a flag)
-----
home_content_aee
Performance & Fast compilation
-----
home_content_aef
Performance
-----
home_content_aeg
C interop without any costs
-----
home_content_aeh
Minimal amount of allocations
-----
home_content_aei
Built-in serialization without runtime reflection
-----
home_content_aej
Compiles to native binaries without any dependencies: a simple web server is only about 250 KB
-----
home_content_afa
As fast as C (V's main backend compiles to human readable C), with equivalent code.
-----
home_content_afb
V does introduce some overhead for safety (such as array bounds checking, GC free), but these features can be disabled/bypassed when performance is more important.
-----
home_content_afc
Fast compilation
-----
home_content_afd
V compiles ≈80k (Clang backend) and ≈400k (x64 and tcc backends) lines of code per second.
-----
home_content_afe
(Apple M2, no optimization)
-----
home_content_aff
V is written in V and compiles itself in under a second (
-----
home_content_afg
0.33s on MacBook Air M3
-----
home_content_afh
Most of the compiler is still single threaded, so it's going to be 2-3x faster in the future!
-----
home_content_afi
Small and easy to build compiler
-----
home_content_afj
V can be bootstrapped in under a second by compiling its code translated to C with a simple
-----
home_content_aga
No libraries or dependencies needed.
-----
home_content_agb
For comparison, space and time required to build each compiler:
-----
home_content_agc
Space
-----
home_content_agd
Build time
